Package: linscp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, python3
Recommends: curl, xdg-utils
Description: graphical and console file transfer client for Linux
 LinSCP is a native noncommercial file transfer client for Linux, inspired
 by WinSCP. It provides an interactive command-line client (linscp) and
 a dual-pane Commander graphical client (linscp-gui) in the browser.
 .
 The desktop entry starts the graphical client through xdg-utils, so
 the browser window is asked for the way a Wayland session expects; without
 xdg-utils the address is printed and nothing is opened.
 .
 SSH, SFTP and SCP are served by libssh and this client's own protocol
 code - the SFTP v3 wire protocol (with the copy-data and check-file-name
 extensions) and, for SCP, the remote-shell directory engine and the rcp
 transfer protocol; ftp, ftps, WebDAV and S3 go through curl, which is why
 it is recommended. The client provides transfer resume and recursive
 synchronization, public-key, ssh-agent and password authentication,
 host-key verification, stored sessions and a subset of WinSCP scripting.
 Protocol support depends on the backend; WebDAV and Amazon S3 support are
 incomplete, and an SCP transfer cannot be resumed, because the rcp
 protocol has no offset to continue from. Full WinSCP feature parity is
 not provided.
